WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.510
SPEAKER: Looking for ways
to easily and securely share

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:07.320
data and insights across
organizational boundaries?

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.060
Give me one minute
and I'll show you

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.760
how with Google
Cloud Analytics Hub.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.370
Analytics Hub is an
exchange platform

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.730
that reduces friction for
publishers and subscribers

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.070
for sharing data,
machine learning models,

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:23.700
and other analytics assets
within a strong security,

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.920
governance, and
privacy framework.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.280
For example, you can augment
your analytics and ML

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.340
initiatives with third
party and Google Data sets.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.620
You can share assets
with your partner network

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.070
or within your own organization,
and if you're a data provider,

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.920
you can build out a
monetization program.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.310
Because it's built on BigQuery,
Google's petabyte-scale cloud

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.820
data warehouse, there are no
servers to deploy or manage

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.670
so administration is a breeze.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.830
As a data publisher,
you can share data

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.770
with as many subscribers
as you want in real time

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:58.080
without having to
replicate your data.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.740
You can quickly build a catalog
of analytics-ready data sources

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.560
with granular permissions
that allow you to deliver data

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.050
to exactly the right audiences.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.420
Then, you can track
and manage subscribers

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.190
and see usage metrics.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.350
As a subscriber,
you can easily find

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.720
the data you're looking
for, combine shared data

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:19.380
with your own, and leverage
the built-in ML, geospatial,

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.650
and natural language
capabilities of BigQuery.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.140
You can take advantage
of the native BI support

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.110
with Looker, Google
Sheets, and Data Studio,

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:31.920
or connect to any of
BigQuery's technology partners.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.890
Analytics Hub is accessible
directly within BigQuery,

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.680
making it easy to
publish, curate, discover,

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.890
and subscribe to the assets
that deliver immediate business

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:41.800
value.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.180
So next time you're looking
to use shared data to drive

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.880
innovation to new
heights, take a minute

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.130
to look at Analytics Hub.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:54.690
To learn more, check out
cloud.google.com/analytics-hub.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:58.040
[MUSIC PLAYING]

